  <page_number>237</page_number>
  <running_head>EVANGELI. SECULI. IV.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Primum est Gen. 3. Adamus fidelis tale</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>peccatum admisit, quo non tantùm se sed</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>omnes omninò involuit, ideoq; gravissimis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>pœnis subjectus fuit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Nihil ad scopum. <i>Primò</i>, Adamus</l>
    <l n="6">&amp; Eva non fuerunt sub federe gratiæ,</l>
    <l n="7">sed operum. <i>Secundò</i>, non habuerunt</l>
    <l n="8">fidem iustificantem, sed generalem</l>
    <l n="9">quoad promissionem benedictionis per</l>
    <l n="10">arborem vitæ designatam. <i>Tertiò</i>, non</l>
    <l n="11">habuerunt promissionem perpetuæ as-</l>
    <l n="12">sistentiæ, ut fideles sub gratiæ federe.</l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="2" para="true">II. Lib. 2. Regum cap. 12.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>David utiq;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>fidelis admisso adulterio &amp; homicidio, suâ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>etiam sententiâ dignum se morte pronun-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>tiat, quam subivisset æternam, nisi pœniten-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>tia peccatum delevisset, Psal. 6. &amp; 37. me-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>ritus est furorem, quem tam calidis lachry-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>mis pœnitentiæq; operibus studet mitigare.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Davidem Regem commisisse pecca-</l>
    <l n="22">tum mortale nos non negamus, neque</l>
    <l n="23">hoc est contra fidei nostræ articulos:</l>
    <l n="24">amisisse</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes />
</page>
